Run the clippy fixer at the exec root

Belongs to rules_lint-no_copy.patch (https://github.com/aspect-build/rules_lint/pull/747):
Without the copy of the sources to the bindir, the fixer must not run there.

`run_patcher` hands `patch_cfg_env` to the fixer it spawns, and the patcher
script (`lint/private/patcher.mjs`) additionally uses `BAZEL_BINDIR` from it as
the prefix under which it expects the files to fix.  Pointing that at the bindir
only works together with `copy_files_to_bin_actions`, which we dropped, so every
clippy finding made `bazel lint` fail with

    Applying Clippy fixes to //packages/check-cert:check-cert-lib failed: (Exit 1)
    Error processing files: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'packages/check-cert/src/lib.rs'

instead of reporting the finding.  The paths in rustc's diagnostics are relative
to the exec root, which is where the unmodified sources are, too, so run the
fixer there.  This gets rid of the hard-coded "../../../" for the diagnostics
file, as well.

diff --git a/lint/clippy.bzl b/lint/clippy.bzl
--- a/lint/clippy.bzl
+++ b/lint/clippy.bzl
@@ -168,8 +168,7 @@
 def _run_patcher(ctx, srcs, rustc_diagnostics_file, patch_file):
     args = [
         "patch",
-        # This path is relative to the execroot, we must relativize it to the bindir.
-        "../../../" + rustc_diagnostics_file.path,
+        rustc_diagnostics_file.path,
     ]
 
     run_patcher(
@@ -180,7 +179,10 @@
         tools = [ctx.executable._rustc_diagnostic_parser],
         files_to_diff = [s.path for s in srcs],
         patch_out = patch_file,
-        patch_cfg_env = {"BAZEL_BINDIR": ctx.bin_dir.path},
+        # The fixer resolves both the diagnostics file and the source paths within
+        # it relative to this directory.  Those paths are relative to the exec
+        # root, and we don't copy the sources to the bindir, either.
+        patch_cfg_env = {"BAZEL_BINDIR": "."},
         env = {},
         mnemonic = _MNEMONIC,
         progress_message = "Applying Clippy fixes to %{label}",
